{"title":"Pyramidal numbers","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The Pyramidal Numbers are the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> which are the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> triangular numbers. The formula for their sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/8/d2870c7df2c42dcce654d25cd79a95c8b4ebd527.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n)(n+1)(n+2)/6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Pyramidal_numbers&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018104301\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.006 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.010 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 16/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 292/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 528/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.658      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.658      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14480:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018104301 and revision id 191342. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}